{
    "id": "YOUR_ACCESS_MODEL_SOD_ANALYSIS_WORKFLOW_ID",
    "name": "Access Model SOD - Analysis",
    "description": "Interactive scan of the access model for intrinsic SoD conflicts. Explains the process, runs custom:access-model-sod-remediation, then reports the outcome. The invoke body is a plain-text NDJSON stream, so every read of it is a string comparison, never a JSONPath into an object.",
    "created": "2026-08-17T10:57:47.039610656Z",
    "modified": "2026-09-22T16:40:00.000000000Z",
    "definition": {
        "start": "Message About This Process",
        "steps": {
            "Message About This Process": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 22px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#0f172a;\">This process inspects the <strong>access model itself</strong>, not people. It looks for roles and access profiles whose own entitlements already sit on both sides of an enforced separation-of-duties policy.</p><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 14px;width:100%;max-width:660px;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1d4ed8;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">1 &middot; What runs</div>Every enabled role in scope is checked against every enforced SoD policy. Nothing in the catalog is changed and no access is revoked.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f0fdf4;border-left:5px solid #16a34a;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#15803d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">2 &middot; What happens to a finding</div>Each new conflict creates a remediation form for the <strong>access item owner</strong>, and <strong>Access Model SOD - Notification</strong> emails them the link. A conflict that already has a form is skipped, so owners are never emailed twice for the same thing.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">3 &middot; While it runs</div>The scan is already running &mdash; this panel is information only and nothing is waiting on you. A large catalog takes several minutes, and the tenant rate limits the API calls behind it. The outcome appears below this panel when it finishes.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Access model SoD analysis"
                },
                "description": "Explains the scan before any tenant API is called.",
                "displayName": "Message: About this process",
                "nextStep": "Configuration",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Configuration": {
                "actionId": "sp:define-variable",
                "attributes": {
                    "id": "sp:define-variable",
                    "variables": [
                        {
                            "description": "ISC API base URL, no trailing slash.",
                            "name": "API URL",
                            "transforms": [],
                            "variableA": "https://tenant.api.identitynow-demo.com"
                        },
                        {
                            "description": "Result source that stores custom operation output.",
                            "name": "SaaS Custom Operations Source Name",
                            "transforms": [],
                            "variableA": "SaaS Custom Operations"
                        },
                        {
                            "description": "Platform connector id for saas-custom-operations.",
                            "name": "SaaS Custom Operations Connector ID",
                            "transforms": [],
                            "variableA": "<CONNECTOR ID>"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                "displayName": "Configuration",
                "nextStep": "Get Access Token",
                "type": "Mutation"
            },
            "Get Access Token": {
                "actionId": "sp:http",
                "attributes": {
                    "formRequestBody": {
                        "grant_type": "client_credentials"
                    },
                    "method": "post",
                    "param_authenticationRef": "basic",
                    "param_basic": {
                        "mapping": {
                            "auth_password": "password",
                            "auth_username": "username"
                        },
                        "paramID": "3e96bf32-75c9-49c0-aa8f-39a688ec733f",
                        "paramType": "1.1",
                        "refID": "026f19db-7950-420f-918d-6b9996325499"
                    },
                    "requestContentType": "form",
                    "url": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/oauth/token"
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Token Failed"
                    }
                ],
                "displayName": "Get Access Token",
                "nextStep": "Call SaaS Custom Operation",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 3
            },
            "Call SaaS Custom Operation": {
                "actionId": "sp:http",
                "attributes": {
                    "jsonRequestBody": {
                        "config": {
                            "apiUrl": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}",
                            "sourceName": "{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsSourceName}}",
                            "token": "{{$.getAccessToken.body.access_token}}"
                        },
                        "connectorRef": "{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsConnectorID}}",
                        "input": {
                            "formName": "Access Model SOD Remediation",
                            "requestId": "access-model-sod-remediation",
                            "scope": "*",
                            "searchIndices": ["roles"]
                        },
                        "tag": "latest",
                        "type": "custom:access-model-sod-remediation"
                    },
                    "method": "post",
                    "param_authenticationRef": "none",
                    "param_basic": {
                        "mapping": {
                            "auth_password": "password",
                            "auth_username": "username"
                        },
                        "paramType": "1.1"
                    },
                    "requestContentType": "json",
                    "requestHeaders": {
                        "Authorization": "Bearer {{$.getAccessToken.body.access_token}}"
                    },
                    "url": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/beta/platform-connectors/{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsConnectorID}}/invoke",
                    "urlParams": {}
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Invoke Error"
                    }
                ],
                "description": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/beta/platform-connectors/{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsConnectorID}}/invoke",
                "displayName": "Call SaaS Custom Operation",
                "nextStep": "Check Invoke Result",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 3
            },
            "Check Invoke Result": {
                "actionId": "sp:compare-strings",
                "choiceList": [
                    {
                        "comparator": "StringContains",
                        "nextStep": "Message Scan Failed",
                        "variableA.$": "$.callSaaSCustomOperation.body",
                        "variableB": "\"status\":\"failed\""
                    }
                ],
                "defaultStep": "Check Violations Found",
                "description": "The connector answers HTTP 200 even when the operation failed, so catch never fires for an operation-level failure. The body is a text/plain NDJSON stream, which is why this is a string check and not a JSONPath read.",
                "displayName": "Invoke failed?",
                "type": "choice"
            },
            "Check Violations Found": {
                "actionId": "sp:compare-strings",
                "choiceList": [
                    {
                        "comparator": "StringContains",
                        "nextStep": "Message No Conflicts",
                        "variableA.$": "$.callSaaSCustomOperation.body",
                        "variableB": "\"access-model-sod-remediation:violations-found\":0"
                    }
                ],
                "defaultStep": "Get Result Source",
                "description": "violations-found is always present in the response summary, and the streamed JSON has no spaces after colons, so a zero result matches this literal exactly.",
                "displayName": "Any conflicts?",
                "type": "choice"
            },
            "Get Result Source": {
                "actionId": "sp:http",
                "attributes": {
                    "method": "get",
                    "param_authenticationRef": "none",
                    "requestHeaders": {
                        "Authorization": "Bearer {{$.getAccessToken.body.access_token}}"
                    },
                    "url": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/v2026/sources",
                    "urlParams": {
                        "filters": "name eq \"{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsSourceName}}\""
                    }
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Conflicts Unavailable"
                    }
                ],
                "description": "Get Accounts filters on source id, and only the source name is configured, so the id is resolved here.",
                "displayName": "Get Result Source",
                "nextStep": "Read Conflict Records",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 3
            },
            "Read Conflict Records": {
                "actionId": "sp:get-accounts",
                "attributes": {
                    "filterCriteria": "sourceId",
                    "getAccountsBy": "filters",
                    "operator": "eq",
                    "value": "{{$.getResultSource.body[0].id}}"
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Conflicts Unavailable"
                    }
                ],
                "description": "One account per conflict that has a remediation form, written by the scan at {requestId}:{accessItemId}:{policyId}. Get Accounts supports only eq and in, so the whole source is read and the loop filters it.",
                "displayName": "Read Conflict Records",
                "nextStep": "Message Conflicts Intro",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Conflicts Intro": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#78350f;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Conflicts found in the access model</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">At least one role or access profile carries entitlements from both sides of an enforced SoD policy. One card follows for each conflict that has a remediation form.</div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 12px;width:100%;max-width:660px;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#1d4ed8;\">Owners already have these</strong> &mdash; <strong>Access Model SOD - Notification</strong> emails the form link when a conflict is first raised. The cards below are for your visibility; you do not need to forward them.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#475569;\">Carried over</strong> &mdash; conflicts raised by earlier scans appear here too. This scan skips them rather than emailing their owners again.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan complete"
                },
                "displayName": "Message: Conflicts intro",
                "nextStep": "Loop Conflicts",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Loop Conflicts": {
                "actionId": "sp:loop:iterator",
                "attributes": {
                    "context.$": "$.trigger",
                    "input.$": "$.readConflictRecords.accounts[?(@.attributes.operationName == 'custom:access-model-sod-remediation')]",
                    "start": "Check Conflict Record",
                    "steps": {
                        "Check Conflict Record": {
                            "choiceList": [
                                {
                                    "comparator": "IsPresent",
                                    "nextStep": "Message Conflict",
                                    "variableA.$": "$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:conflicting-entitlements-group-a']"
                                }
                            ],
                            "defaultStep": "End Step - Success",
                            "description": "The scan also writes an account on the bare requestId when an invoke fails. That record carries no conflict detail and is skipped here.",
                            "displayName": "Has a form?",
                            "type": "choice"
                        },
                        "Message Conflict": {
                            "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                            "attributes": {
                                "category": "INFO",
                                "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.loop.context.interactiveProcessId",
                                "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:22px 24px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Conflict</div><div style=\"font-size:19px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#78350f;margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><a href=\"{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:access-item-url']}}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#78350f;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#d97706;text-underline-offset:3px;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:access-item-name']}}</a></div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">Its own entitlements sit on both sides of <strong><a href=\"{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:policy-url']}}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#1d4ed8;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:policy-name']}}</a></strong>, so anyone granted it breaches the policy on day one.</div></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#64748b;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">What collides</div><table role=\"presentation\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:14px 0;width:100%;max-width:688px;margin:0 0 22px -14px;table-layout:fixed;\"><tr><td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding:0;\"><div style=\"background-color:#fff1f2;border-left:5px solid #e11d48;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be123c;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Group A</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;word-break:break-word;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:conflicting-entitlements-group-a']}}</div></div></td><td width=\"50%\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:50%;vertical-align:top;padding:0;\"><div style=\"background-color:#eef2ff;border-left:5px solid #4f46e5;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4338ca;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Group B</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;word-break:break-word;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:conflicting-entitlements-group-b']}}</div></div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 20px 12px 0;vertical-align:top;width:190px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#64748b;\">Type</td><td style=\"padding:12px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#0f172a;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:access-item-type']}}</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 20px 12px 0;vertical-align:top;width:190px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#64748b;\">Policy</td><td style=\"padding:12px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#0f172a;\"><a href=\"{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:policy-url']}}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#1d4ed8;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:policy-name']}}</a></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 20px 12px 0;vertical-align:top;width:190px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#64748b;\">Owner notified</td><td style=\"padding:12px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#0f172a;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:form-email-recipients'][0]}}</td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 18px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The owner holds a remediation form for this conflict and chooses which side to correct. The link is in their email and is deliberately not repeated here, since it only works for them.</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:#94a3b8;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;word-break:break-all;\">{{$.loop.loopInput.nativeIdentity}}</div>",
                                "ownerId.$": "$.loop.context.launchedBy.id",
                                "title": "{{$.loop.loopInput.attributes['access-model-sod-remediation:access-item-name']}}"
                            },
                            "displayName": "Message: Conflict",
                            "nextStep": "End Step - Success",
                            "type": "action",
                            "versionNumber": 1,
                            "description": "Reads the persisted conflict detail and links the catalog definitions. No form link: the launcher is rarely the form recipient."
                        },
                        "End Step - Success": {
                            "displayName": "",
                            "type": "success"
                        }
                    }
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Conflicts Unavailable"
                    }
                ],
                "description": "One panel per conflict. Outer state reaches loop steps only through context, so the interactive process and launcher are passed that way.",
                "displayName": "Loop: Conflicts",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Success",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Conflicts Unavailable": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#78350f;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Conflicts found, but the list could not be loaded</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The scan itself completed and any new remediation form was created and emailed to its owner. Only this read-back of the stored records failed.</div></td></tr></table><div style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">Check that the result source named in Configuration exists and that the token may read its accounts. The owner emails are unaffected.</div>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan complete"
                },
                "displayName": "Message: Conflicts unavailable",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Success",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message No Conflicts": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f0fdf4;border-left:5px solid #16a34a;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#15803d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#14532d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">No conflicts in the scanned access model</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">Nothing in scope puts an enforced SoD policy on both sides of the same role or access profile. No remediation form was created and no owner was emailed.</div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 12px;width:100%;max-width:660px;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#1d4ed8;\">What this covers</strong> &mdash; the access model itself. Conflicts an identity picks up by combining separate access items are handled by <strong>SOD Violation - Notification</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#475569;\">Scope</strong> &mdash; only the roles and policies selected on the invoke step were read. Widening <code>scope</code> or <code>searchIndices</code> there widens the scan.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan complete"
                },
                "description": "Zero-violation outcome. No record is written for a clean scan, so there is nothing to read back.",
                "displayName": "Message: No conflicts",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Success",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Scan Failed": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "ERROR",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fef2f2;border-left:5px solid #dc2626;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b91c1c;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#7f1d1d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">The scan stopped before it finished</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The connector answered, but the operation reported a failure. Findings from this run are incomplete, and the catalog was not changed.</div></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#64748b;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Operation response</div><div style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 20px;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;\">{{$.callSaaSCustomOperation.body}}</div><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 12px;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:18px 0 0 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#b45309;\">HTTP 429</strong> &mdash; the tenant rate limited the scan. Narrow <code>scope</code> or <code>searchIndices</code> on the invoke step, or run it again when the tenant is quieter.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#475569;\">Anything else</strong> &mdash; check the Configuration values and the token scopes. Forms already created by earlier runs are untouched, and a re-run skips conflicts that already have one.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan did not complete"
                },
                "description": "Operation-level failure. The body carries the error text, which is the only place the cause appears.",
                "displayName": "Message: Scan failed",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Failure",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Invoke Error": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "ERROR",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
